    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e83d5bab_12104bd3",
        "filename": "zephyr/shim/include/zephyr_host_command.h",
        "patchSetId": 16
      },
      "lineNbr": 71,
      "author": {
        "id": 1438457
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-07-28T08:07:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This whole complexity is introduced, because tests call the `host_command_process` function directly. The response buffer is passed to `host_command_process` via `args`. On the other hand, the upstream uses internal buffers, which are passed to the command handlers.\n\nSome tests check the exact pointer of the used response buffer - if it matches the buffer passed via `host_command_process`, so the response buffer passed to the command handler is replaced here - `host_command_get_response_buf` to get it.\n\nTo reflect the real system as much as possible, content of the response buffer passed by the upstream (internal buffer) is copied to the buffer used by the command handler (the one passed via `host_command_process`). As you said, the buffer passed by the upstream should be zeroed at this point and `memcpy` is added to catch if it\u0027s not.",
      "parentUuid": "6ac1f164_e23c2516",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 71,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "75167f772d242d7ffdde2dcf9e9f6d6f9f9abdbe",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
